<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Decolonisation</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Decolonisation refers to the process by which colonies gained independence from imperial powers, especially in the decades after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>. It brought the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire">French Empire</a> as global colonial systems, and the defeat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a> in 1945 likewise freed its former colonies. The process reshaped the political map of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>.</p></div>
